% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-24 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: acquired micronutrient cytopenia with myeloneuropathy
%   (the workup of progressive pancytopenia + peripheral neuropathy in a
%   post-bariatric, daily-zinc-supplementing adult), NOT a single diagnosis.
%
% The central diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q5): a 54-year-old man with
% progressive PANCYTOPENIA (anemia + neutropenia, platelets relatively
% preserved early), MACROCYTOSIS, bilateral foot paresthesias (a myelo-
% neuropathy), marrow showing dyserythropoiesis, ring sideroblasts, and
% PROMINENT CYTOPLASMIC VACUOLIZATION of erythroid AND myeloid precursors,
% with NO clonal cytogenetic abnormality -- in the setting of a sleeve
% bariatric operation, past heavy alcohol use, prior low zinc, and
% UNINTERRUPTED daily over-the-counter zinc supplementation. A presumptive
% myelodysplastic-syndrome (MDS) label was applied and transplant pursued.
%
% That conjunction -- vacuolated marrow precursors + ring sideroblasts +
% neutropenia-with-preserved-platelets + a copper-lowering exposure (zinc) and
% a malabsorptive anatomy (bariatric) + B12-like myeloneuropathy -- is the
% textbook picture of ZINC-INDUCED COPPER DEFICIENCY masquerading as MDS.
%
% Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (no leading digit,
% no uppercase identifiers). E.g. marrow_vacuolization(prominent),
% platelets(relatively_preserved), neutrophils(severely_reduced).
%
% Anti-overfit note: every clause is added because a cited source supports the
% DIRECTION of the likelihood ratio for that finding in that disease, NOT to
% make this case land on a chosen answer. Discriminators that argue AGAINST the
% tempting wrong answer (MDS) carry LR<1 wherever a source supports them.
% Correlated findings that are ONE mechanism (the copper-deficiency
% marrow/blood gestalt) are grouped under a single mechanism directive so the
% combined likelihood ratio fires ONCE and does not double-count.
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates among unexplained-cytopenia / suspected-MDS workups) =====

% rationale: among adults referred for progressive cytopenias with dysplastic
% marrow, MDS is the common, "default" working diagnosis -- which is exactly why
% it was the presumptive label here; high prior so the engine must EARN the move
% away from it on the copper-deficiency-specific data.
prior 0.34 for diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "CAP 2023 What's New in MDS (ICC vs WHO5): cytopenias + marrow dysplasia define MDS" trust authoritative

% rationale: zinc-induced copper deficiency is an under-recognized but well-
% described reversible MDS mimic; in a patient with BOTH a malabsorptive
% bariatric anatomy AND uninterrupted daily zinc, its pretest probability is high.
prior 0.30 for diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "Karger Case Rep Oncol 2023;16:55 (Copper Deficiency Mimicking MDS, zinc supplementation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: vitamin B12 deficiency causes macrocytic anemia + cytopenias + a
% subacute-combined-degeneration myeloneuropathy and was the prior misattribution
% (he had received B12 repletion); kept on the differential.
prior 0.12 for diagnosis(vitamin_b12_deficiency)
  source "ASH Blood 2017;129:2603 (B12 deficiency from the perspective of a hematologist)" trust authoritative

% rationale: chronic heavy alcohol use suppresses marrow and causes macrocytosis
% with cytopenias; a plausible contributor given his past heavy alcohol use.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(alcohol_related_marrow_suppression)
  source "StatPearls NBK459295 Macrocytic Anemia (alcohol: direct marrow toxicity, macrocytosis)" trust authoritative

% ===== SHARED COPPER-DEFICIENCY MARROW/BLOOD SIGNATURE (ONE mechanism) =====
% rationale: the constellation -- cytoplasmic vacuolization of erythroid AND
% myeloid precursors, ring sideroblasts, dyserythropoiesis, neutropenia with a
% relatively preserved platelet count, and macrocytic anemia -- is ONE correlated
% syndrome (the hematologic phenotype of hypocupremia), NOT several independent
% facts. Counting each separately would double-count correlated evidence and
% saturate the posterior, so it fires ONCE as a single combined likelihood ratio.
% mechanism hypocupremic_marrow_phenotype for diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy) lr 9.0 : marrow_vacuolization(prominent), marrow_ring_sideroblasts(present), neutrophils(severely_reduced), platelets(relatively_preserved), anemia(macrocytic)

% rationale: the SAME marrow picture is precisely what fools observers into an MDS
% diagnosis, so several of these features are weakly consistent with MDS too -- but
% as ONE correlated cluster, at a much SMALLER combined LR than for copper
% deficiency, and offset by the negative discriminators below.
% mechanism dysplastic_overlap_phenotype for diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome) lr 2.0 : marrow_vacuolization(prominent), marrow_ring_sideroblasts(present), neutrophils(severely_reduced), anemia(macrocytic)

% ===== COPPER DEFICIENCY MYELONEUROPATHY (zinc-induced) =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR -- cytoplasmic vacuolization of erythroid AND myeloid
% precursors is regarded as characteristic of copper deficiency and, unlike MDS, is
% the feature that distinguishes the two on the aspirate. Kept as an independent
% edge ON TOP of the shared mechanism because sources single it out as the most
% specific morphologic clue.
contributes 4.0 from marrow_vacuolization(prominent) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "Wiley Clin Case Rep 2015 (Dalal): cytoplasmic vacuoles in erythroid+myeloid precursors characteristic of Cu deficiency" trust authoritative

% rationale: daily uninterrupted over-the-counter zinc is the classic, sufficient
% cause -- excess zinc induces enterocyte metallothionein that traps dietary copper,
% producing acquired hypocupremia. This is the single most specific exposure clue.
contributes 6.0 from exposure(daily_zinc_supplementation) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (Copper deficiency: excess zinc, metallothionein, treat by stopping zinc)" trust consensus

% rationale: a prior gastric/bariatric (sleeve) operation is a recognized
% malabsorptive cause of acquired copper deficiency, independent of the zinc.
contributes 2.5 from history(bariatric_surgery) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "ScienceDirect 2025 (severe copper-deficiency polyneuropathy after laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a B12-like myeloneuropathy -- bilateral foot paresthesias / sensory
% disturbance -- is the cardinal neurologic manifestation of acquired copper
% deficiency and clusters with the cytopenias as a shared etiology.
contributes 3.0 from symptom(peripheral_neuropathy) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "MedLink Neurology, Copper deficiency myeloneuropathy (foot/hand paresthesias, dorsal-column sensory ataxia)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ABSENCE of clonal cytogenetic abnormality is expected in copper
% deficiency (a non-clonal, reversible mimic) and supports it over true MDS.
contributes 1.8 from cytogenetics(normal_no_clonal_abnormality) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "PMC4427377 (Copper deficiency mimicking MDS: no cytogenetic abnormality, unlike MDS)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a falling marrow cellularity to HYPOcellular with persistent
% dyserythropoiesis but NO progression to blasts, and worsening counts off any
% disease-directed therapy, fits a continuing nutritional insult rather than clonal
% evolution.
contributes 1.5 from marrow_course(hypocellular_no_blast_excess) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "PMC5290493 (copper-deficiency marrow changes: dysplasia without blast excess, reversible)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY SYNERGY -- the characteristic vacuolization together with the
% copper-lowering zinc exposure is near-specific for hypocupremia; the morphology
% plus the mechanism reinforce each other beyond their separate weights.
interacts 3.0 when marrow_vacuolization(prominent) and exposure(daily_zinc_supplementation) for diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "Karger Case Rep Oncol 2023;16:55 (zinc-induced copper deficiency: vacuolated precursors + zinc source)" trust authoritative

% ===== MYELODYSPLASTIC SYNDROME (the presumptive label -- must be argued DOWN) =====

% rationale: ring sideroblasts are a recognized morphologic feature of MDS-RS, the
% reason the marrow was read as dysplastic. Real positive edge, but non-specific --
% copper deficiency produces them too.
contributes 1.6 from marrow_ring_sideroblasts(present) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "ASH Blood 2015;126:233 (SF3B1 / ring sideroblasts define an MDS-RS subset)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- a contemporary MDS-RS diagnosis leans
% on a clonal marker (SF3B1) or a clonal cytogenetic abnormality. A marrow with NO
% clonal cytogenetic abnormality argues against clonal MDS and toward a reactive
% mimic.
contributes 0.45 from cytogenetics(normal_no_clonal_abnormality) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "CAP 2023 (ICC/WHO5: MDS-RS rests on SF3B1 / a defining clonal lesion)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- a clearly REVERSIBLE exposure (daily
% zinc) that itself explains the whole marrow picture lowers the probability that
% the cytopenias are clonal MDS; copper deficiency must be excluded before an MDS
% label.
contributes 0.30 from exposure(daily_zinc_supplementation) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "Haematologica 2018 (copper deficiency: important consideration in differential of MDS)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- prominent cytoplasmic vacuolization of
% precursors is NOT typical of MDS and specifically points away from it.
contributes 0.40 from marrow_vacuolization(prominent) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "PMC4427377 (vacuolization within precursors distinguishes copper deficiency FROM MDS)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR -- copper deficiency characteristically SPARES platelets
% (neutropenia with preserved platelets); preserved platelets early is therefore a
% soft argument against the more typically tri-lineage clonal MDS.
contributes 0.7 from platelets(relatively_preserved) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "Wiley AJH 2020;95 (hematologic effects of copper deficiency: anemia+neutropenia, platelets preserved)" trust authoritative

% ===== VITAMIN B12 DEFICIENCY (the prior misattribution) =====

% rationale: macrocytic anemia with cytopenias and a peripheral neuropathy is the
% classic B12-deficiency presentation, which is why B12 was repleted earlier.
contributes 1.5 from anemia(macrocytic) to diagnosis(vitamin_b12_deficiency)
  source "AAFP 2003 Vitamin B12 Deficiency (macrocytic anemia, neuropathy)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.4 from symptom(peripheral_neuropathy) to diagnosis(vitamin_b12_deficiency)
  source "MSD Manual, Vitamin B12 Deficiency (subacute combined degeneration, paresthesias)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- a serum B12 MARKEDLY ELEVATED above
% the assay ceiling, on supplementation, makes an ACTIVE B12-deficient state the
% cause of these ongoing cytopenias improbable. (An elevated level does not perfectly
% exclude functional deficiency, so the LR is small but not zero.)
contributes 0.20 from serum_b12(markedly_elevated) to diagnosis(vitamin_b12_deficiency)
  source "ASH Blood 2017;129:2603 (elevated B12 does not confirm sufficiency, but high level argues against active deficiency)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- prior B12 repletion already given,
% with continued deterioration, argues against unresolved B12 deficiency as the
% driver of the worsening counts.
contributes 0.5 from prior_treatment(b12_repletion_given) to diagnosis(vitamin_b12_deficiency)
  source "AAFP 2003 (treating B12 deficiency corrects anemia; persistence despite repletion argues against)" trust authoritative

% ===== ALCOHOL-RELATED MARROW SUPPRESSION =====

% rationale: chronic alcohol causes macrocytosis and marrow suppression, so
% macrocytic anemia fits a remote alcohol contribution.
contributes 1.4 from anemia(macrocytic) to diagnosis(alcohol_related_marrow_suppression)
  source "StatPearls NBK459295 Macrocytic Anemia (alcohol-related macrocytosis, marrow toxicity)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- alcohol-related marrow changes
% improve with abstinence; heavy use is described as PAST, and ring sideroblasts +
% precursor vacuolization point at a trace-metal etiology rather than active
% ethanol toxicity.
contributes 0.5 from marrow_vacuolization(prominent) to diagnosis(alcohol_related_marrow_suppression)
  source "Wiley Clin Case Rep 2015 (vacuolated precursors are the copper-deficiency, not alcohol, signature)" trust inferred

% ===== NEXT STEP (the conspicuously missing trace-metal labs) =====

% rationale: the decisive next step is a serum COPPER + CERULOPLASMIN + ZINC panel:
% low copper and ceruloplasmin with high zinc confirm zinc-induced copper deficiency
% and separate it from MDS. These trace-metal labs are conspicuously absent from the
% workup.
prior 0.30 for next_step(serum_copper_ceruloplasmin_zinc_panel)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (low serum copper + low ceruloplasmin establish deficiency; check zinc for cause)" trust consensus
contributes 5.0 from exposure(daily_zinc_supplementation) to next_step(serum_copper_ceruloplasmin_zinc_panel)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (serum zinc may be high if zinc excess is the cause -> order the panel)" trust consensus
contributes 4.0 from marrow_vacuolization(prominent) to next_step(serum_copper_ceruloplasmin_zinc_panel)
  source "Haematologica 2018 (vacuolated precursors should prompt copper studies before an MDS label)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from history(bariatric_surgery) to next_step(serum_copper_ceruloplasmin_zinc_panel)
  source "ScienceDirect 2025 (post-sleeve copper deficiency -> measure copper/ceruloplasmin)" trust authoritative

% rationale: the alternative confirmatory arm if a clonal process is still feared --
% molecular / SF3B1 + repeat cytogenetics to settle MDS vs mimic. Lower prior because
% the reversible-exposure data point at the metal panel first.
prior 0.12 for next_step(marrow_molecular_sf3b1_cytogenetics)
  source "CAP 2023 (SF3B1 sequencing + cytogenetics establish/exclude clonal MDS-RS)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from marrow_ring_sideroblasts(present) to next_step(marrow_molecular_sf3b1_cytogenetics)
  source "ASH Blood 2015;126:233 (ring sideroblasts -> test SF3B1 to define MDS-RS)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved -- the missing labs) =====

% u-copper: serum copper / ceruloplasmin has not been measured. A LOW result is
% near-dispositive for copper deficiency; a NORMAL result argues strongly against and
% back toward MDS. This is the highest-value-of-information item.
contributes 12.0 from serum_copper(low) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (low serum copper + ceruloplasmin establish copper deficiency)" trust consensus
contributes 0.12 from serum_copper(normal) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "PMC4427377 (normal copper/ceruloplasmin argues against copper-deficiency mimic)" trust authoritative
uncertain { serum_copper(low), serum_copper(normal) } for diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (serum copper/ceruloplasmin not yet measured; decisive discriminator)"

% u-copper vs MDS: the same copper result swings MDS the other way -- a LOW copper
% pulls the explanation away from clonal MDS; a NORMAL copper leaves MDS standing.
contributes 0.15 from serum_copper(low) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "Haematologica 2018 (a documented copper deficiency reclassifies the cytopenias as a reversible mimic)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.5 from serum_copper(normal) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "CAP 2023 (with reversible causes excluded, dysplastic cytopenias support MDS)" trust authoritative
uncertain { serum_copper(low), serum_copper(normal) } for diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (copper studies pending; result reclassifies MDS vs mimic)"

% u-trial: a copper-repletion / zinc-cessation trial has not been done; a
% hematologic response within weeks confirms copper deficiency, non-response argues
% against it.
contributes 8.0 from copper_repletion_response(hematologic_recovery) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (hematologic abnormalities normalize within ~1 month of copper repletion)" trust consensus
contributes 0.2 from copper_repletion_response(no_recovery) to diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "Wiley AJH 2020;95 (failure to recover with copper repletion argues against copper deficiency)" trust authoritative
uncertain { copper_repletion_response(hematologic_recovery), copper_repletion_response(no_recovery) } for diagnosis(copper_deficiency_myeloneuropathy)
  source "CMAJ 2025;197:E456 (empiric copper repletion + zinc cessation not yet trialed)"
